This release contains only the standalone PyTorch implementation of BiFlow
(`biflow.py`) and a minimal usage example.

It does not contain:

- the Ultralytics integration layer;
- the training or evaluation pipeline;
- the TOD dataset;
- trained checkpoints or ONNX files in the source repository.

The paper checkpoints are distributed as a separate release asset, described
in `weights/README.md`. The baseline detector used in the paper is built on
Ultralytics, which is distributed under its own license. The integration layer
is not part of this standalone release.
